<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Britain</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Britain, or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-great-britain">Great Britain</a>, is an island off northwestern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> comprising <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>, united as a single kingdom from 1707. It was a province of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> and later the metropolitan centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a>, the largest empire in history. As a leading naval, commercial and industrial power, Britain was a rival or partner of the French, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a>, German and Russian empires and intervened in the affairs of many others.</p></div>
